    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented a daily-limit rule on `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RequireCityCapacity`/`CityAtCapacity` pattern), I added:\n\n1. **`RequireDailyOwnerLimit.java`** \u2014 pipeline step that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count reaches the limit of 100.\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception carrying the date.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 escalation handler responding `429` with an `errors: [\"registrationDate\"]` body.\n4. **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `dailyLimit` step (transaction-governed) between `cityCapacity` and `build`.\n\nNew owners default to today's date in `BuildOwner`, so the check runs before the entity is built and blocks further creates once the day is full. The acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100, expects the 101st to get 429) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
